  "findings": [
    "Batch barrier consumed385completed-slotseconds; removing it eliminated that wait and passed18000buyers at60/s300s without customer drops/errors/caller retries.",
    "Callback backlog peak409to65 and due-to-callback proxy p957695to490ms. APIpool mean8.37to2.84ms; first-attempt customer503s46to0. No DB ceiling/transport/SQL/consumer/polling change.",
    "Refill observed one failed simulator HTTP delivery, subsequently recovered by existing lease/redelivery semantics; do not claim every internal attempt was error-free.",
    "Fresh paid/unpaid postTTL,zero duplicates/extra paid events/fullqueues/Kafka/source/restore/idle/privatecleanup passed in botharms. Batch customer verdict remainsFAILED; refillPASSED."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Five minutes with isolated300-seatshows establishes this workload, not hourly or hot-concert capacity. A60tickets/s average extrapolation is216000/hour, below300000/hour; no hourly claim.",
    "Worst child p95 is not a combined percentile; phase histograms use upper bucket bounds. Claim means include empty polls. DBtimestamps are statement proxies, not commit timers.",
    "Actual downstream request volume changes with fulfillment speed; freshfixture identities/history remain uncontrolled. Simulator is development-only; real provider capability is separate."
  ],
